# Secrets — NEVER commit (rulebook App.A rule 39-40, guidelines §7.4)
.env
.env.*
!.env-example
credentials.json
token.json
*credentials*.json
*token*.json
*.key
*.pem
/config/game.toml
/config/*.local.toml

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
.uv-cache/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
dist/
build/
*.egg-info/

# Generated runtime artifacts
/logs/
/reports/generated/
/results/generated/

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/

# Google OAuth client files. Rule 39 (Prohibited) forbids pushing secrets "even if it is
# private and shared only with the lecturer"; the sanction is severe security failure and
# project failure. `token.json` and `credentials.json` were already covered, but the Google
# Cloud console downloads the client as
# `client_secret_<id>.apps.googleusercontent.com.json`, which matches neither pattern --
# so the one file a user actually receives from Google was the one that would be committed.
# Found 2026-08-07 while wiring the reporting credential.
client_secret*.json
*client_secret*.json
*.apps.googleusercontent.com.json
service_account*.json
*service-account*.json
*.pem
